  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Community Voices for Equitable and Sustainable Finance in Ghana</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Will engage in: (1) Capacity development of Civil Society Organisations (CSOs) and Community Based Organisations (CBOs) on sustainable, equitable and well -regulated financial institutions and companies. (2) Awareness creation on community and legal rights and entitlements for CBOs related to Free Prior Informed Consent (FPIC) and fair compensation. (3) Public interest and strategic litigation support to affected communities for redress to rights violations. (4) Media and investigative journalism. (5) Legal literacy for CBOs in mining host communities/enclaves. (6) Policy dialogue and engagement with companies, financial institutions and government regulators. (7) Community -led evidence gathering of human rights violations by companies.  Undertake two (2) case studies on the impact for communities of gold mines and a planned lithium mine. One policy assessment will be carried out, covering banks who are active and signatories to the 2019 Ghana Sustainable Banking Principles and Sector Guidance Notes as well as banks which are present in both Ghana and Nigeria.</narrative>
  </description>
